body:
I know the proposal suggested it, but I really don't think using JSON for serialization here is a good idea. While the conversion is benign when merely copy/pasting to other editor instances, trying to work with data outside of the editor becomes more frustrating as a result, and I think that would go against the spirit of the proposal.

For example, my biggest sore spot and use case for such a feature is editing resource and scene files manually in a text editor. Say I want to take a position I grabbed from one scene and copy it to a several other scenes, but without having to open each scene in the editor. I'd like copying the property's value to the OS clipboard to give me: `Vector2(2.549, 3.104)`. But this PR would give me: `{"type": "Vector2", "args": [2.549, 3.104]}`.

Reformatting that to paste into a Godot resource is not the worst thing to deal with but the problem greatly compounds with nested structures: 

```tres
{
  "player": {
    "position": Vector2(5, 8),
    "tags": ["hero", 42]
  }
}
```
becomes
```json
{
  "type": "Dictionary",
  "args": [
    "s:player", {
      "type": "Dictionary",
      "args": [
        "s:position", {"type": "Vector2", "args": [5, 8]},
        "s:tags", {
          "type": "Array",
          "args": ["s:hero", "i:42"]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

There's a reason Godot rolls its own serialization for Variants in its TRES/TSCN text resources: it ends up being a lot easier to read, understand, and modify when you're outside the editor, while preserving important type information while necessary. It's purpose-built -- other standard seralized formats are naturally going to be far more verbose and less readable in order to retain the same information. 

In my opinion, `JSON.[from/to]_native` exists solely for transferring data to/from systems that have no understanding of Godot types. Given that limited use case for the average developer task, and given Godot already has a variant-to-text serializer, I think this PR ends up feeling too narrow and feel it wouldn't meet the proposal's goals.

I'd really like to see a version of this PR that makes use of Godot's existing text-based serializer. Either way, it may still be nice to provide the option to transfer data to/from JSON for one-off operations involving cases that require cooperation with outside systems. However, I'd highly suggest treating it as separate and distinct from copying a property value, and treat it more as a conversion operation:
- Bring the copy and paste JSON options into their own section in the context menu.
- Rename them to "Copy Value to JSON" and "Paste Value from JSON"?
- Remove the setting to copy JSON to the OS clipboard via the default "Copy Value" option, or in the very least turn it off by default, since data conversions should be opt-in.

I appreciate you tackling one of my constant sore spots with the engine 🙏
